args: opentide --json serve --help
exit: 0

━━━ stdout
Run CLI commands in one warm process, for editors

JSON-RPC 2.0 on stdio, one message per line. Each run request executes a
command as opentide --json would and answers with its document and exit
code, without starting a new process each time; the read-only commands
keep the workspace loaded between runs. The editor owns the process: it
ends on exit or when stdin closes. stdout carries the protocol only; logs
go to stderr.

Usage: opentide serve

Options:
      --help
          Print help

Examples:
  $ opentide serve

━━━ stderr · empty
